#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""P2-16 (a0 source half, a4 run half) -- THE CONSTRAINT DEPTH IS RETIRED, NOT DEFAULTED OFF.

`spallation.sp.constraint_depth` (P2-2e; carried onto the face list in P2-14a) is deleted. `spallation.*` sits
outside any strict ParmParse scope and ALAMO does not abort on an unused top-level key (standing rule 1), so a
deleted parse alone would leave every study argv that sets d running SILENTLY with d ignored. The retired-key list
in MMWSpalling::Parse is the only guard; this test proves it from both sides.

Source half (comments included: a leftover NAME in a comment is a leftover too, as in P2-10's clause):
  R1 none of the deleted names (sp_cref_d, CrefInterp, CrefTAtDepth, BuildConstraintRefColumns, cref_n_*,
     T_cref, run_ref, Tref_at, cref_on) appears anywhere in src/
  R2 the key string appears in src/ exactly ONCE, in the P2-16 retired-key list, and that list runs in Parse
     before any key is queried
  R3 its abort names the key (the loop variable) and P2-16
  R4 P2-10's retired-key list is intact (three probes) and its message unchanged
  R5 (P2-20) the typed beam absorption is gone: no `alpha_parser` / `alpha_f` identifier anywhere in src/; MMWBeam.H
     has no parser (no `registerVariables`, no `amrex::Parser`) and no `alpha_expr` / `R` query; it parses
     beam.eps_r and beam.tan_delta AFTER lambda and forms alpha and R from them; the key strings "beam.alpha_expr"
     and "beam.R" each appear in src/ exactly ONCE, in the P2-20 list, which runs before the beam parse.
     (Restated from the packet's "none of alpha_expr ... registerVariables in MMWSpalling.H": seven unrelated
     parsers there call registerVariables legitimately, and the key string must survive in the abort list.)
  R6 (P2-21, P2-20 review DR-2) THE ASSOCIATION LOCK: MMWBeam.H forms alpha verbatim as
     `2.0 * M_PI * std::sqrt(v.eps_r) * (v.tan_delta / v.lambda)` -- the one order in which every beam-ON
     fixture's tan_delta string reproduces its old typed alpha bit for bit (studies/p2_20_beam_deposition/Z0.txt);
     an algebraically equal reassociation moves the frozen gate decks. Exactly one `v.alpha = ` assignment.
  R7 (P2-26, census B3) the four top-level keys of the closed switches retired AT A DEFAULT -- spall.flake_length
     (twocell), spall.flake_fraction (cf), weibull.size_volume (cell), weibull.V_ref (*) -- each appear in src/
     exactly ONCE (comments included), as an entry of the retired-at-default table with that value
  R8 (P2-26, census C2 + C3) the same for spall.surface_normal (0), spall.flake_coherence_length (0),
     spall.melt_aware (0) and melt.lambda_crit (*). Until P2-27 the "0" was compared as a STRING, so a deck writing
     0.0 aborted (P2-26 DR-3: 622 record argvs); since P2-27 a one-token number is compared as a double (K14-K16)
  R9 (P2-27, census C1a) THE DAMAGE LINEAGE IS DELETED: no identifier of the Drucker-Prager damage law, the cohesive
     zone, the damage-law removal (the C_h sqrt(alpha t) thickness, the principal-stress ratio, spall.sample's scan
     windows, the prescribed ratio) or the damage_law model value survives anywhere in src/ (comments included);
     src/Numeric/DruckerPrager.H and CohesiveZone.H are gone; the three table keys (damage.enabled 0,
     conductivity.kappa_damage_alpha 0.0, spall.sample top_cell) each appear in src/ exactly ONCE, as their
     retired-at-default entry; the P2-27 abort list names the eight spall.* keys once each and the two families
     damage.* / cohesive.*
Each clause has a MUTATION that must turn it RED, and the full revert turns every clause RED. With --pre <dir>
(MMWSpalling.H, Removal.H, FaceRemoval.H, and MMWBeam.H when present, substituted for their src/ copies) the
clauses named by --red (default R1,R2,R3: P2-16's pre-change copy) must be RED and every other one GREEN; P2-20's
pre-change copy is checked with --red R5.

Run half (bin/mmwspalling-3d-g++, the gradient_blind fixture, ONE step of 0.008 s, -np 1):
  K1 + spallation.sp.constraint_depth=0  -> rc != 0, output names the key and P2-16 (the former DEFAULT value,
     so an abort can only mean "the key is gone", never "the value was refused")
  K2 + spall.lateral_drive=0             -> rc != 0, output names the key and P2-10 (the old list still works)
  K3 + beam.alpha_expr=10                -> rc != 0, output names the key and P2-20 (P2-20; the beam is OFF here)
  K4 + beam.R=0.0                        -> rc != 0, output names the key and P2-20
  K0 the fixture alone                   -> rc == 0 (or "aborts" would hold for a binary refusing every deck)
  P2-26 (census B3; the retired-at-default table, P2-18's pattern):
  K5 + the four B3 keys at their defaults -> rc == 0 (a kept deck naming them at the old default still runs)
  K6 + spall.flake_length=flux           -> rc != 0, output names the key and P2-26
  K7 + weibull.size_volume=flux          -> rc != 0, output names the key and P2-26
  K8 + spall.flake_fraction=weibull      -> rc != 0, output names the key and P2-26
  K9 + surface_patch.pad_shield_open=0.5 -> rc != 0, the strict surface_patch scope names the key (unparsed)
  P2-26 (census C2 + C3):
  K10 + the four C2/C3 keys at their old defaults (0, 0, 0, 0.4) -> rc == 0
  K11 + spall.surface_normal=1           -> rc != 0, output names the key and P2-26
  K12 + spall.flake_coherence_length=0.004 -> rc != 0, output names the key and P2-26
  K13 + spall.melt_aware=1               -> rc != 0, output names the key and P2-26
  P2-27 (the numeric compare; K12 above is the live value that still aborts):
  K14 + spall.flake_coherence_length=0.0 -> rc == 0 (0.0 equals the table's "0" as a number; aborted until P2-27)
  K15 + spall.surface_normal=0.0 and spall.melt_aware=0.0 -> rc == 0
  K16 + spall.flake_coherence_length="0 0" (TWO tokens) -> rc != 0: only a ONE-token number is compared as a double
  P2-27 stage 2 (census C1a, the damage lineage):
  K17 + damage.enabled=0 + conductivity.kappa_damage_alpha=0.0 + spall.sample=top_cell -> rc == 0 (the defaults)
  K18 + damage.enabled=1                 -> rc != 0, names the key and P2-27 (retired at its default)
  K19 + spallation.model=damage_law      -> rc != 0, names damage_law and P2-27
  K20 + damage.ic.type=expression        -> rc != 0, names the key and P2-27 (the damage.* family)
  K21 + spall.sample=shallow_max         -> rc != 0, names the key and P2-27
  K22 + cohesive.enabled=0               -> rc != 0, names the key and P2-27 (the cohesive.* family, any value)
  K23 + spall.xi_s=8.0                   -> rc != 0, names the key and P2-27
  K24 + microstructure.phase0.A_D=0.0    -> rc == 0;  K25 + microstructure.phase0.A_D=0.5 -> rc != 0, names P2-27
  K26 + spallation.model=none            -> rc != 0: the explicit `none` with spall.enabled = 1 is refused (removal
       needs the sp_weibull criterion since the damage-law removal is gone)

Usage: test [--source | --run] [--pre <dir> [--red R5,...]]     (default: both halves)
"""
import os
import re
import subprocess
import sys
import tempfile

HERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))
ROOT = os.path.abspath(os.path.join(HERE, "..", "..", "..", ".."))
SRC = os.path.join(ROOT, "src")
KEY = "spallation.sp.constraint_depth"
DELETED = re.compile(r"\b(?:sp_cref_d|CrefInterp|CrefTAtDepth|BuildConstraintRefColumns|T_cref|run_ref|"
                     r"Tref_at|cref_on|cref_on_sp)\b|\bcref_n_\w+")
SUBST = {"MMWBeam.H": os.path.join("Numeric", "MMWBeam.H"),
         "MMWSpalling.H": os.path.join("Integrator", "MMWSpalling.H"),
         "Removal.H": os.path.join("Integrator", "MMWSpalling", "Removal.H"),
         "FaceRemoval.H": os.path.join("Integrator", "MMWSpalling", "FaceRemoval.H")}


def read_src(pre=None):
    """{relpath under src/: text} for every C++ source; under --pre the three headers come from <pre>"""
    out = {}
    for dp, _d, fs in os.walk(SRC):
        for fn in fs:
            if fn.endswith((".H", ".h", ".cpp", ".cc")):
                p = os.path.join(dp, fn)
                out[os.path.relpath(p, SRC)] = open(p, errors="replace").read()
    if pre:
        for fn, rel in SUBST.items():
            if os.path.exists(os.path.join(pre, fn)):
                out[rel] = open(os.path.join(pre, fn)).read()
    return out


MMW = SUBST["MMWSpalling.H"]
# P2-26: the keys retired AT A DEFAULT, per clause (the retired-at-default table, MMWSpalling::Parse)
P2_26 = {"R7": {"spall.flake_length": "twocell", "spall.flake_fraction": "cf",
                "weibull.size_volume": "cell", "weibull.V_ref": "*"},
         "R8": {"spall.surface_normal": "0", "spall.flake_coherence_length": "0",
                "spall.melt_aware": "0", "melt.lambda_crit": "*"}}


# P2-27 (census C1a): THE DAMAGE LINEAGE -- identifiers (comments included) that must be gone from src/
C1A = re.compile(r"\b(?:ParseDamageSettings|DamageGrowthRHS|IntegrateDamageRK4|UpdateDamageAfterMechanics|"
                 r"ParseCohesiveSettings|UpdateCohesiveAfterMechanics|ResetCohesiveDiagnostics|PrincipalStressRatio|"
                 r"SpallSampleMode|DamageLaw|damage_enabled|cohesive_enabled|(?<!\.)kappa_damage_alpha|"
                 r"damage_(?:phi_deg|phi_rad|cohesion|alpha_dp|k_dp|psi0|n|m|gb_multiplier|stiffness_floor)|"
                 r"damage_(?:F|Psi|rate)_mf|damage_prescribed_stress_enabled|damage_s(?:xx|yy|zz|xy|yz|zx)_(?:parser|f)|"
                 r"cohesive_(?:K_n|delta_c|delta_max|prescribed_enabled|delta_parser|delta_f)|"
                 r"gb_(?:delta|delta_max|traction|cohesive_damage)_mf|"
                 r"spall_(?:damage_threshold|xi_s|C_h|alpha_override|alpha|t_spall_override|t_spall|"
                 r"prescribed_ratio_enabled|ratio_parser|ratio_f|sample_mode|shallow_depth)|DruckerPrager|CohesiveZone)\b")
P2_27_TABLE = {"damage.enabled": "0", "conductivity.kappa_damage_alpha": "0.0", "spall.sample": "top_cell"}
P2_27_SPALL = ["spall.alpha", "spall.C_h", "spall.t_spall", "spall.damage_threshold", "spall.xi_s",
               "spall.shallow_depth", "spall.prescribed_ratio.enabled", "spall.prescribed_ratio.expr"]


def clauses(src):
    out = []

    def need(name, ok):
        out.append((name, bool(ok)))

    left = ["%s:%d" % (rel, ln) for rel, t in src.items()
            for ln, line in enumerate(t.split("\n"), 1) if DELETED.search(line)]
    need("R1 no deleted constraint-depth name anywhere in src/ (%d line(s)%s)"
         % (len(left), (": " + ", ".join(left[:4])) if left else ""), not left)

    m = src[MMW]
    total = sum(t.count(KEY) for t in src.values())
    body = re.search(r"static void Parse\(MMWSpalling& value, IO::ParmParse& pp\)\s*\{([\s\S]*?)\n    \}\n", m)
    body = body.group(1) if body else ""
    lst = re.search(r'for \(const char\* k : \{"%s"\}\)\s*if \(pp\.contains\(k\)\)\s*Util::Abort\(INFO, k,'
                    % re.escape(KEY), body)
    first_q = re.search(r"pp\.(?:query|queryclass|select|get|contains\(\"(?!%s))" % re.escape(KEY),
                        body[:lst.start()] if lst else "")
    # the P2-10 loop's own `pp.contains(k)` is the only query allowed before it
    pre_q = [x for x in re.finditer(r"pp\.\w+\(", body[:lst.start()] if lst else "")
             if not x.group(0).startswith("pp.contains(")]
    need("R2 the key appears in src/ exactly once, in the P2-16 retired-key list, which runs in Parse before any "
         "key is queried (%d occurrence(s))" % total,
         total == 1 and lst is not None and not pre_q and first_q is None)

    msg = re.search(r'for \(const char\* k : \{"%s"\}\)[\s\S]*?remove "\s*"it from the input"\);' % re.escape(KEY), m)
    need("R3 the abort names the key (the loop variable k) and P2-16",
         msg is not None and "P2-16" in msg.group(0) and "Util::Abort(INFO, k," in msg.group(0))

    probes = ['"spall.lateral_drive"', '"surface_patch.side_face_flux"', '"surface_patch.jet_wall_march"']
    need("R4 P2-10's retired-key list is intact (3 probes) and its message unchanged",
         all(m.count(p) == 1 for p in probes)
         and 'was retired in P2-10 (the flame wall machinery: "' in m)

    bm = src[SUBST["MMWBeam.H"]]
    bm_code = "\n".join(l.split("//")[0] for l in bm.split("\n"))
    idents = sum(len(re.findall(r"\b(?:alpha_parser|alpha_f)\b", t)) for t in src.values())
    nstr = {k: sum(t.count('"%s"' % k) for t in src.values()) for k in ("beam.alpha_expr", "beam.R")}
    lst20 = re.search(r'for \(const char\* k : \{"beam\.alpha_expr", "beam\.R"\}\)\s*if \(pp\.contains\(k\)\)'
                      r'\s*Util::Abort\(INFO, k, " was retired in P2-20', m)
    i_beam = m.find('pp.queryclass<Numeric::MMWBeam>("beam"')
    i_lam = bm_code.find('pp.query_default("lambda"')
    i_eps = bm_code.find('pp.query_default("eps_r"')
    i_td = bm_code.find('pp.query_default("tan_delta"')
    i_a = bm_code.find("v.alpha = ")
    i_r = bm_code.find("v.R = ")
    need("R5 (P2-20) no alpha_parser/alpha_f in src/ (%d); MMWBeam.H has no parser and no alpha_expr/R query; "
         "eps_r, tan_delta parsed after lambda, alpha and R formed after both; each key string once (%s), in the "
         "P2-20 list before the beam parse" % (idents, nstr),
         idents == 0 and "registerVariables" not in bm_code and "amrex::Parser" not in bm_code
         and '"alpha_expr"' not in bm_code and 'query_default("R"' not in bm_code
         and 0 <= i_lam < i_eps < i_td < min(i_a, i_r) and i_a >= 0 and i_r >= 0
         and nstr == {"beam.alpha_expr": 1, "beam.R": 1} and lst20 is not None and 0 <= lst20.start() < i_beam)

    want = "v.alpha = 2.0 * M_PI * std::sqrt(v.eps_r) * (v.tan_delta / v.lambda);"
    n_assign = len(re.findall(r"\bv\.alpha\s*=[^=]", bm_code))
    need("R6 (P2-21) MMWBeam.H forms alpha in the locked association `%s` (%d assignment(s) of v.alpha)"
         % (want[10:-1], n_assign), bm_code.count(want) == 1 and n_assign == 1)

    tab = re.search(r"static const RetiredAtDefault retired_at_default\[\] = \{([\s\S]*?)\n        \};", m)
    tab = tab.group(1) if tab else ""
    for tag, keys in P2_26.items():
        cnt = {k: sum(t.count(k) for t in src.values()) for k in keys}
        inn = {k: re.search(r'\{"%s",\s*"%s",' % (re.escape(k), re.escape(v)), tab) is not None
               for k, v in keys.items()}
        need("%s (P2-26) each key string appears in src/ exactly once, as its retired-at-default entry with the "
             "old default (%s)" % (tag, ", ".join("%s %d%s" % (k, cnt[k], "" if inn[k] else " NOT IN TABLE")
                                                 for k in keys)),
             all(c == 1 for c in cnt.values()) and all(inn.values()))
    # P2-27 R9 (census C1a): the damage lineage
    left9 = ["%s:%d" % (rel, ln) for rel, t in src.items()
             for ln, line in enumerate(t.split("\n"), 1) if C1A.search(line)]
    hdrs = [h for h in ("Numeric/DruckerPrager.H", "Numeric/CohesiveZone.H") if h in src]
    cnt9 = {k: sum(t.count('"%s"' % k) for t in src.values()) for k in P2_27_TABLE}
    inn9 = {k: re.search(r'\{"%s",\s*"%s",' % (re.escape(k), re.escape(v)), tab) is not None
            for k, v in P2_27_TABLE.items()}
    lst27 = re.search(r"P2-27 \(census C1a\)[\s\S]*?for \(const char\* k : \{([^}]*)\}\)", m)
    keys27 = re.findall(r'"([\w.]+)"', lst27.group(1)) if lst27 else []
    fam = all(('"%s"' % f) in m for f in ("damage", "cohesive")) and "P2-27" in m
    # damage.enabled appears TWICE by design: its table row, and the family loop's exemption `k != "damage.enabled"`
    want9 = {k: (2 if k == "damage.enabled" else 1) for k in P2_27_TABLE}
    exempt = 'k != "damage.enabled"' in m
    need("R9 (P2-27) no damage-lineage identifier in src/ (%d line(s)%s), DruckerPrager.H / CohesiveZone.H gone (%s); "
         "the three table keys in the table, once each (damage.enabled twice: + the family exemption) (%s); the P2-27 "
         "list names the eight spall.* keys (%d) and the damage / cohesive families"
         % (len(left9), (": " + ", ".join(left9[:4])) if left9 else "", hdrs or "gone",
            ", ".join("%s %d%s" % (k, cnt9[k], "" if inn9[k] else " NOT IN TABLE") for k in P2_27_TABLE), len(keys27)),
         not left9 and not hdrs and cnt9 == want9 and exempt and all(inn9.values())
         and sorted(keys27) == sorted(P2_27_SPALL) and fam)
    return out


def _mmw(fn):
    return lambda s: dict(s, **{MMW: fn(s[MMW])})


MUTATIONS = [
    ("R1", "plant the member `Set::Scalar sp_cref_d = 0.0;` back",
     _mmw(lambda t: t.replace("    Set::Scalar sp_buckle_span = 0.0;",
                              "    Set::Scalar sp_cref_d = 0.0;\n    Set::Scalar sp_buckle_span = 0.0;", 1))),
    ("R2", "re-add the parse of the key (a second occurrence, which would run with it read)",
     _mmw(lambda t: t.replace('        pp.query_default("spall.buckle_span"',
                              '        { Set::Scalar d0 = 0.0; pp.query_default("%s", d0, 0.0); }\n'
                              '        pp.query_default("spall.buckle_span"' % KEY, 1))),
    ("R3", "the message stops naming P2-16",
     _mmw(lambda t: t.replace(" was retired in P2-16 (the constraint depth", " was retired (the constraint depth", 1))),
    ("R4", "drop one P2-10 key from its list",
     _mmw(lambda t: t.replace('                                "spall.lateral_drive",\n', "", 1))),
    ("R5", "plant the typed-alpha executor `amrex::ParserExecutor<1> alpha_f;` back in MMWBeam.H",
     lambda s: dict(s, **{SUBST["MMWBeam.H"]: s[SUBST["MMWBeam.H"]].replace(
         "    std::vector<Set::Scalar> sched_t;", "    amrex::ParserExecutor<1> alpha_f;\n    std::vector<Set::Scalar> sched_t;", 1)})),
    ("R6", "reassociate alpha to left-to-right `2 pi sqrt(eps_r) tan_delta / lambda` (algebraically equal)",
     lambda s: dict(s, **{SUBST["MMWBeam.H"]: s[SUBST["MMWBeam.H"]].replace(
         "std::sqrt(v.eps_r) * (v.tan_delta / v.lambda);", "std::sqrt(v.eps_r) * v.tan_delta / v.lambda;", 1)})),
    ("R7", "re-add the parse of spall.flake_length (a second occurrence of the key string)",
     _mmw(lambda t: t.replace('        pp.query_default("spall.flake_c_f"',
                              '        { std::string fl; pp.query_default("spall.flake_length", fl, std::string("twocell")); }\n'
                              '        pp.query_default("spall.flake_c_f"', 1))),
    ("R9", "plant the member `bool damage_enabled = false;` back",
     _mmw(lambda t: t.replace("    Set::Scalar sp_buckle_span = 0.0;",
                              "    bool damage_enabled = false;\n    Set::Scalar sp_buckle_span = 0.0;", 1))),
    ("R8", "re-add the parse of spall.melt_aware (a second occurrence of the key string)",
     _mmw(lambda t: t.replace('        pp.query_default("spall.flake_c_f"',
                              '        { int mo = 0; pp.query_default("spall.melt_aware", mo, 0); }\n'
                              '        pp.query_default("spall.flake_c_f"', 1))),
]


def source_half(pre):
    src = read_src()
    bad = 0
    print("SOURCE HALF (a0) -- POST-CHANGE src/ (must be GREEN):")
    res = clauses(src)
    for nm, ok in res:
        print("  %s  %s" % ("ok  " if ok else "FAIL", nm))
        bad += 0 if ok else 1
    print("\nMUTATION CONTROLS (each must turn its own clause RED):")
    s_all = src
    for tgt, label, fn in MUTATIONS:
        s2 = fn(src)
        changed = s2 != src
        rr = dict((k.split()[0], v) for k, v in clauses(s2))
        was = dict((k.split()[0], v) for k, v in res).get(tgt, False)
        ok = changed and was and not rr.get(tgt, True)
        print("  %s  %s: %s" % ("ok  " if ok else "FAIL", label,
              "source unchanged" if not changed else (tgt + (" goes RED" if not rr.get(tgt, True) else " STAYS GREEN"))))
        bad += 0 if ok else 1
        s_all = fn(s_all)
    still = [k.split()[0] for k, v in clauses(s_all) if v]
    print("  %s  full revert of every mutation: %s" % ("ok  " if not still else "FAIL",
          "every clause RED" if not still else "still GREEN: " + ", ".join(still)))
    bad += 1 if still else 0
    if pre:
        red = (sys.argv[sys.argv.index("--red") + 1] if "--red" in sys.argv else "R1,R2,R3").split(",")
        rp = clauses(read_src(pre))
        print("\nPRE-CHANGE headers (%s) -- %s must be RED, every other clause GREEN:" % (pre, ",".join(red)))
        for nm, ok in rp:
            want = nm.split()[0] not in red
            print("  %s  %s" % (("GRN " if ok else "RED ") + ("    " if ok == want else "!!  "), nm[:100]))
            bad += 0 if ok == want else 1
    return bad


def leg(extra):
    d = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="retkey_")
    argv = ["mpirun", "--oversubscribe", "--bind-to", "none", "-np", "1",
            os.path.join(ROOT, "bin", "mmwspalling-3d-g++"),
            os.path.join(ROOT, "tests", "MMWSpalling", "unit", "gradient_blind", "input")] + extra + \
           ["stop_time=0.008", "plot_file=%s" % os.path.join(d, "run")]
    r = subprocess.run(argv, cwd=ROOT, capture_output=True, text=True)
    return r.returncode, (r.stdout or "") + (r.stderr or "")


def run_half():
    bad = 0
    print("RUN HALF (a4) -- one step of the gradient_blind fixture, -np 1:")
    for tag, extra, want_abort, names in (
            ("K1", ["%s=0" % KEY], True, [KEY, "P2-16"]),
            ("K2", ["spall.lateral_drive=0"], True, ["spall.lateral_drive", "P2-10"]),
            ("K3", ["beam.alpha_expr=10"], True, ["beam.alpha_expr", "P2-20"]),
            ("K4", ["beam.R=0.0"], True, ["beam.R", "P2-20"]),
            ("K0", [], False, []),
            ("K5", ["spall.flake_length=twocell", "spall.flake_fraction=cf", "weibull.size_volume=cell",
                    "weibull.V_ref=1.0e-9"], False, []),
            ("K6", ["spall.flake_length=flux"], True, ["spall.flake_length", "P2-26"]),
            ("K7", ["weibull.size_volume=flux"], True, ["weibull.size_volume", "P2-26"]),
            ("K8", ["spall.flake_fraction=weibull"], True, ["spall.flake_fraction", "P2-26"]),
            ("K9", ["surface_patch.pad_shield_open=0.5"], True, ["surface_patch.pad_shield_open",
